{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"WAVE 3 REBAR ARM CLOSED. All nine three-arm Wave 3 runs now carry a completed supplementary rebar panel (three independent classifiers each, majority-aggregated): 27 classifiers, 107 findings. Pooled precision 93.2 percent, materiality 68 percent, recall 16 percent, 14 rebar-unique true positives, 188 of 223 adjudicated true positives missed, zero contested items. Figures reported earlier in the session were superseded as panels closed and are recorded as such rather than replaced: precision 100 to 95.5 to 94.2 to 93.2; rebar-unique 6 to 14 to 13 to 14; materiality 77 to 79 to 71 to 68. The spread across runs matters more than the pooled mean: ruby-oscer-member-facing-status scored 22 true positives of 23 items while js-gutenberg scored 2 with 8 nits and nothing unique, same tool and settings. The three nit-heaviest runs are exactly the three whose acceptance criteria the harness copied or lifted; the two runs with verbatim criteria produced 1 and 2 nits. Scaffolding quality, not reviewer capability, is the dominant variable in rebar's Wave 3 performance."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789442962698239001,"uuid":"9a253e7b-2b4d-4654-9109-93a6ab05f68e"}